WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
MELISSA NOBLES: Here,
our mission at MIT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.590
is to apply knowledge
gained through research

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.100
to solve the world's
most pressing problems.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.690
And we cannot do that without
scientists from historically

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.430
marginalized communities.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.260
MONIQUE EARL-LEWIS: We want
education to be accessible.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.790
We want it to be free.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.070
We want it to be open.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.400
And we want it to reflect the
communities in which people

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.070
serve, people learn,
and people teach.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.080
ROBBIE MELTON: We
are now in a climate

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.250
where people are trying to limit
when you learn, how you learn,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.180
and what you learn.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.980
I'm here to promote OER,
Open Education Resources.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.520
And open education
means exactly that.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.577
It's open.

00:00:42.577 --> 00:00:44.160
JEAN-JACQUES MEDASTIN:
OER means to me

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.360
that it is possible for
somebody who looks like me,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.580
came from the same world as
I did to achieve something

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.990
that they never dreamed of.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.790
It's accessibility.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.960
It's freedom.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.110
It's-- its gift.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.530
It means the world to me.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.450
And that's why I'm so excited.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:06.600
I'm like, this is possible.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.220
This is finally possible.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.820
ROBBIE MELTON: You have three
powerful forces coming together

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.830
again, the HBCUs,
and MIT, Merlot.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:23.670
The need is worldwide
for people of all races,

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:28.980
underrepresented populations to
be able to access information,

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:34.170
and to tap in to rich
cultural resources

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.525
to help them in their
academic journey.

00:01:36.525 --> 00:01:39.150
MONIQUE EARL-LEWIS: There is no
one-size-fits all in education.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.670
We have very different
and unique experiences

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.910
in terms of our histories,
our culture, our education,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.130
our disciplines, but
we're finding ways

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.500
to connect the values
and goals that we

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.620
have that will benefit
not only the students

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.800
at our institution, but
institutions, faculty,

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.640
and students around the world.

